================================================================================
2. QUOTE DATASET — CC BY-NC-SA 2.5
================================================================================

Applies to quotes.csv, and NOT to any of the code above.

The quotations were crowd-sourced by readers of the Guardian in 2011 and
assembled by Jaap Meijers into the original literary clock dataset. They are
licensed Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 2.5:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.5/

This means the dataset — including this repository's corrected and extended
version of it — may be shared and adapted for non-commercial purposes, with
attribution, and any redistribution must carry the same license.

The quotations themselves are excerpts from copyrighted works, reproduced here
in the brief, transformative manner the original project established. The
copyright in each excerpt remains with its respective rightsholder.

Corrections and additions in this repository draw on the dataset's community
forks, which carry the same license:

    https://github.com/JohannesNE/literature-clock
    https://github.com/cdmoro/literature-clock
    https://github.com/kapoorankush/litclock


================================================================================
3. THIRD-PARTY FILES
================================================================================

usr/local/stuff/bin/stuff.sh is a lightly modified copy of a file from
NiLuJe's Kobo usbnet/KoboStuff package, tracked here for reference so the boot
hook is documented. It is not this project's work and is redistributed under
its original terms:

    https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=254214

The FBInk binary and the NotoSerif fonts the scripts call at runtime live on
the device, not in this repository. FBInk is by NiLuJe (GPLv3+, with an
AGPLv3+ option); Noto fonts are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
